# ~/.config/camtrap/telegram.env — mode 600, and the agent REFUSES to read it otherwise.
#
# This file is the one place the laptop holds a Telegram token, and it exists because the owner
# decided on 2026-09-03 that clips should be sent from the laptop directly, overriding the rule in
# SPEC section 8 that had kept the token off this machine.
#
# USE A BOT OF ITS OWN — not the one the Pi uses. This is not tidiness, it is the mitigation for
# the actual risk: a bot can delete its own messages for 48 hours, so a token on a machine assumed
# to be in a thief's hands means whoever carries the laptop out can clear what that bot sent. With
# a separate bot that is the clips only, and the photographs — which arrive through the Pi's bot,
# whose token never leaves home — cannot be touched from the laptop at all.
#
# The deployment of 2026-09-03 declined this and uses the shared bot; SPEC section 8 records what
# that widens. The advice below is still the advice for any fresh install.
#
#   1. talk to @BotFather, /newbot, take the token
#   2. send that new bot one message from the account that should receive the clips
#   3. put the token below, and the same chat id the Pi uses
#
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=000000:replace-me-with-a-bot-of-its-own
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=000000000
